<title>USA: Becton Dickinson to sell $200 mln in debt.</title>
<headline>Becton Dickinson to sell $200 mln in debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Becton Dickinson and Co is expected to sell $200 million in a debt offering via sole manager Goldman Sachs &amp; Co, dealers said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The A1/A-plus rated deal is expected to include a 30-year noncallable maturity, dealers said.</p>
<p>Becton Dickinson makes medical, diagnostic products and hospital supplies.</p>
<p>(( -- U.S. corporate bond unit, 212-859-1675 ))</p>
